#: 54e81fe4971a4bd48f97979c60401b42
msgid "In ``dom0``, enable the formula for ``sys-gui-gpu`` with pillar data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:81
#: 007f1917e2b04d60bb9cba4b7a5d6542
msgid "You can now disable the ``sys-gui-gpu`` formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:88
#: 9d7d02b8ff674afeadda183f0c7a319e
msgid ""
"One more step is needed: attaching the actual GPU to ``sys-gui-gpu``. This "
"can be done either manually via ``qvm-pci`` (remember to enable permissive "
"option), or via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:95
#: 16588a2d34aa4c69b3d34dec8d09ff0f
msgid ""
"The latter option assumes Intel graphics card (it has hardcoded PCI "
"address). If you don’t have Intel graphics card, please use the former "
"method with ``qvm-pci`` (see :doc:`How to use PCI devices </user/how-to-"
"guides/how-to-use-pci-devices>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:97
#: ff7d4812a604494fa33abe1582026b66
msgid ""
"**Note:** Some platforms can have multiple GPU. For example on laptops, it "
"is usual to have HDMI or DISPLAY port linked to the secondary GPU (generally "
"called *discrete GPU*). In such case, you have to also attach the secondary "
"GPU to ``sys-gui-gpu`` with permissive option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:99
#: a9f8005329074eb0aedf5241bb3d80ec
msgid ""
"At this point, you need to reboot your Qubes OS machine in order to boot "
"into ``sys-gui-gpu``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:101
#: ed906d1e46084cbb9acb4facff4703d4
msgid ""
"**Note:** For some platforms, it can be sufficient to shutdown all the "
"running qubes and starting ``sys-gui-gpu``. Unfortunately, it has been "
"observed that detaching and attaching some GPU cards from ``dom0`` to ``sys-"
"gui-gpu`` can freeze computer. We encourage reboot to prevent any data loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:103
#: a7cbdd1a13084b3691cdb08d73ed59cd
msgid ""
"Once, ``lightdm`` is started, you can log as ``user`` where ``user`` refers "
"to the first ``dom0`` user in ``qubes`` group and with corresponding "
"``dom0`` password. A better approach for handling password is currently "
"discussed in `QubesOS/qubes-issues#6740 <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-"
"issues/issues/6740>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:106
